{
 "summary": "Checkout latency is rising with no errors. p95 near the end of the window was about 923ms at gateway, 933ms at orders and 738ms at inventory, all with a 0% 5xx ratio. Inventory was deployed 3.1.5 -> 3.2.4 at 10:03:21Z, mid-window, which makes it the leading suspect, but there are no traces, logs or baseline to confirm where the time is spent.",
 "root_cause": {
  "statement": "Likely a latency regression in inventory 3.2.4, deployed at 10:03:21Z. Latency is elevated in inventory and in its likely callers, orders and gateway. This is not confirmed: no trace self-time, logs or pre-deploy baseline link the deploy to the slowdown, and the metrics show no detected latency onset.",
  "service": "inventory",
  "confidence": "low",
  "evidence_ids": [
   "ev-3723edf2d58b",
   "ev-cf2f8c523735",
   "ev-ab523774f133",
   "ev-475f30836653"
  ]
 },
 "contributing_factors": [
  {
   "statement": "Inventory p95 latency rose to about 740ms (avg 447ms, last 738ms). That would account for most of the orders and gateway p95 if those services call inventory synchronously.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-cf2f8c523735",
    "ev-ab523774f133",
    "ev-475f30836653"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "The last p95 reading is well above the window average for every service (gateway 923ms vs 571ms; orders 933ms vs 555ms; inventory 738ms vs 447ms), so latency was still worsening at the end of the window.",
